# Crovion — static export on Apache / LiteSpeed shared hosting (Hostinger).
#
# Copied from public/ into out/ by `next build`, so it lands in public_html/
# with the rest of the site. Kept to directives shared hosting allows in
# .htaccess: anything it refuses turns the whole site into a 500.
#
# HTTPS is deliberately not forced here. Use hPanel's "Force HTTPS" switch:
# a rewrite rule that checks %{HTTPS} can loop behind a CDN or proxy that
# talks to this server over plain HTTP.

# A directory resolves to its index.html (`trailingSlash: true` emits
# out/privacy/index.html for /privacy). Listed first so a leftover index.php
# from a previous site can't take precedence.
DirectoryIndex index.html

# The site's own not-found page instead of the host's.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html

# Every JS, CSS and font file the build emits lives under /_next/static/ with a
# content hash in its name, so a changed file is a new URL and the old one can
# be cached for good. HTML is left alone so a redeploy shows up immediately.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css|woff2)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
